exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__pixellab__animate_image_pixminimax(args: {
  // The motion (e.g. 'walking forward', 'flame flickering', 'chest opening'). Describe movement, not appearance.
  description: string;
  // Facing of the sprite (south = towards the camera), the model's facing caption field. Omit to have it read from the image.
  direction?: "south" | "north" | "east" | "west" | "south-east" | "south-west" | "north-east" | "north-west";
  // True rewrites a short description ('shooting a bow') as PixMiniMax's action caption before generating (+0.05 generations); the rewritten text is returned.
  enhance_prompt?: boolean;
  // Base64 PNG to animate — the first frame. Max 256x256. PREFER first_frame_url; MCP clients routinely truncate large inline base64.
  first_frame_base64?: string | null;
  // Alternative to first_frame_base64: an https, data: or `upload:<id>` URL to the first frame PNG. PREFER THIS. Give one, not both.
  first_frame_url?: string | null;
  // Frames to generate, a multiple of 4 from 4 to 40 at any size up to 256x256. 4 for idle loops, 8 for walk/run, 16+ for complex actions.
  frame_count?: number;
  // The pose the first frame is in (e.g. 'standing upright with the sword lowered'). Omit to have it read from the image.
  initial_pose?: string | null;
  // Optional final frame, same size as the first, to pin where the motion ends.
  last_frame_base64?: string | null;
  // Alternative to last_frame_base64: an https, data: or `upload:<id>` URL to the final frame PNG. Give one, not both.
  last_frame_url?: string | null;
  // True (default) returns the frames on transparency; an opaque input is cut out of its first frame before animating. False keeps an opaque backdrop.
  no_background?: boolean;
  // Internal Game Builder project context; the finished image is linked after generation.
  project_id?: string | null;
  // Seed for reproducible generation.
  seed?: number | null;
  // What the first frame shows, one noun phrase (e.g. 'a knight in silver plate armour'). Omit to have it read from the image.
  subject_description?: string | null;
  // Camera view of the sprite, the model's view caption field. Omit to have it read from the image.
  view?: "low top-down" | "high top-down" | "side";
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```

Add an animation to an existing, completed object. Returns one queued job per
direction at once (~30-60s each, pixminimax ~1-7 min). Poll with get_object.

For a character (create_character) use animate_character; for an image that is
not a PixelLab object, animate_image.

Modes:
- v3 (default): from animation_description; usually best and cheapest.
- pixminimax (beta): longer clips, frames a multiple of 4 up to 40.
- pro: a different style. Its first call returns the price; re-call with
  confirm_cost=True only after the user agrees.

1-direction objects animate their one facing; 8-direction objects all 8 unless
you pass directions. To add directions to an animation, pass its
animation_group_id (from get_object) and the mode it was made with. A start or
end frame needs exactly one direction. Palette is pro only;
max_colors is Pro-only too.

Cost: v3 ceil(width x height x frames / 65536) per direction, minimum 1: 48x48
or 64x64 at 8 frames = 1, 96x96, 128x96 or 128x128 = 2; width x height x frames
is capped at 524,288. pixminimax: 64x64 at 4/8/16/40 frames = 1/1/2/6 per
direction. pro: 10-25 per direction (80-200 for all 8).

Full reference (frame rules per mode, keyframes, direction prompts):
search_help(tool="animate_object").

